1. Seismic and geographic data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

private/jma-stations.json
private/snet_stations.json
public/japan-regions.geojson
public/tsunami-regions.geojson

    Derived from observation point and area-code information published by the
    Japan Meteorological Agency (気象庁 / JMA).
    https://www.jma.go.jp/

    JMA content is generally published under the Government of Japan Standard
    Terms of Use (Version 2.0), which permits reproduction and redistribution,
    including for commercial purposes and in modified form, with attribution.
    Those terms are broadly compatible with CC BY 4.0.
    https://www.jma.go.jp/jma/kishou/info/coment.html

private/nied_stations.json

    Derived from observation point information published by the National
    Research Institute for Earth Science and Disaster Resilience
    (国立研究開発法人防災科学技術研究所 / NIED), operators of the Kyoshin
    Monitor real-time seismic intensity service.
    https://www.bosai.go.jp/  |  http://www.kmoni.bosai.go.jp/

Real-time observation data

    Fetched at runtime from the Kyoshin Monitor service operated by NIED, and
    from JMA telegrams delivered via the DMDATA / DM-DSS service
    (https://dmdata.jp/), which requires a paid subscription. No such data is
    redistributed in this repository. Users of a WebQuake deployment obtain
    this data under their own subscription and under the terms of the
    respective operators.

Kyoshin Monitor colour-scale conversion

    The algorithm converting Kyoshin Monitor tile colours back to seismic
    intensity values is derived from a method published on Qiita, attributed
    inline in the source where it is implemented.

